From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:17:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Decide governance requests that cross into StegVerse-Labs
 over InTr

StegCore is a StegVerse-Labs repository, so a governance decision belongs
here. Another organization emits the request through its own .github egress;
it crosses Interlock/InTr on the federation mesh and is received here.

- services.json declares stegverse-labs.governance, an INTERNAL_ENDPOINT with
  an admitted adapter, admitting governance on the canonical governed route.
- The kernel dispatches an INTERNAL_ENDPOINT that declares an admitted
  adapter. The adapter is resolved before any receipt is minted, receipts use
  the same receipt rule as every role so the origin recomputes the chain, and
  the adapter runs under the kernel's own interpreter. Boundary-local roles
  are unchanged.
- governance_endpoint.py decides the request with StegCore's StegGate and
  records the decision at both ledger levels in this organization. A request
  that does not recompute, cannot be evaluated, or arrives where StegCore is
  not materialized is decided FAIL_CLOSED, naming why.

Tested by tests/test_governance_endpoint.py (8 tests, stub StegCore) and
end to end against StegVerse-org/.github with StegCore ef38410: DENY,
signal.inputs_incomplete, admitted by the SDK as ORGANIZATION_RECORDS_ONLY.

